// Test build, and why it exists in this shape.
//
// `ui/` had no test runner at all before 2026-09-01: CI ran eslint, tsc and
// `next build`, and the §4.6 crypto in lib/archive-key.ts — the one part of
// this frontend where a silent mistake costs an operator their archive — was
// covered by nothing. Adopting a disk now decrypts in the browser, and
// "unlocking with the wrong passphrase fails visibly" is a claim that has to be
// executed rather than asserted in a comment.
//
// The runner is `node --test`, which ships with Node and adds NOTHING to
// package.json. That mattered more than the ergonomics of a framework: §4.6's
// hash-wasm approval was explicitly conditioned on the dependency being scanned
// (storage.md §4.6), against a ui/ whose npm packages were read by no scanner
// at the time. Answering "we need tests" with forty more unscanned packages is
// the wrong trade to make quietly. If a component-rendering framework is wanted
// later, that is a dependency decision to take on its own merits.
//
// `module: commonjs` is the load-bearing setting. The lib sources import each
// other WITHOUT file extensions (`./passphrase-kdf`), which Node's ESM resolver
// refuses and its CommonJS resolver handles — so tsc emits CJS into .test-out/
// and node runs that. hash-wasm ships a UMD main, so it requires cleanly too.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": false,
    "module": "commonjs",
    "moduleResolution": "node",
    "outDir": ".test-out",
    "incremental": false,
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  "include": ["lib/**/*.ts", "components/storage/*.ts"]
}
